;| ; A document whose one anchor is an INLINE `.mid` — the shape every bound
;| ; SMF operation is exercised against (plan 07, "Bound content,
;| ; precisely"). The anchor carries its dump, so the file is never read
;| ; FOR its content.
;| ;
;| ; `x.mid` IS beside it, all the same: plan 02 verifies an anchor's `:size`
;| ; and `:sha256` before it honours a single offset, and a case with no file
;| ; would load with `anchor_unavailable`. `zig build fixtures` writes it as
;| ; the canonical write of exactly the module spelled below, so the file and
;| ; the dump are one thing said twice and a drift between them is loud. This
;| ; is one of the two bound cases `tempura edit` itself drives
;| ; (`src/cli/edit.zig`'s tests and the CLI goldens).
;| ;
;| ; One track at 480 PPQ with three notes on channel 1 and a controller the
;| ; `filter` lane reads: a note whose neighbours leave it room to move in
;| ; place, one that has to cross the controller to reach its destination,
;| ; and two `(control-change …)` events so a curve lane has steps of its
;| ; own. `spare` is native and empty, which is what a `bind` needs.
;| (timeline :title "bound" :conductor song :length 2bar)
;|
